ontratos junto al límite se reparten entre 201 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.876,03 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: La concentración de contratos al límite no refleja actos ilícitos. Puede deberse a precios de mercado o necesidades específicas. No implica que se haya partido ningún contrato ni que haya existido malversación.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en otros años. Analizar si los contratos al límite coinciden con presupuestos cerrados o ajustes de gasto.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 244 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 58.6 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 4.2, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.5 to 5.0. December accounts for 8% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 7% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 5. Contract [1], for 14,876.03 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper activity. Similar distribution could result from routine scheduling. The number of awardees does not prove any single contract was improperly structured.\nWhat can be checked: Check if December contracts were for the same service to avoid duplication. Review awardee A's contracts to ensure no single provider was overused. Contract [1] should be examined for its specific service to confirm it aligns with the body's needs.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["VDjCcbz4f0YeC9GJQOEBkQ%3D%3D","5420M35g4S9rSd8H4b2soA%3D%3D","ZiKw%2B9F97kYZDGvgaZEVxQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"